> what is the log of 8?
  note: "log" without a base: log base 2 (kept for this session)
  ucas: log(8)/log(2)
3
> what is the log of 1024?
  ucas: log(1024)/log(2)
10
> what is the range of x for a byte x?
  note: "byte" without signed or unsigned: signed, i8 (kept for this session)
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x
  ucas: range it
range of it -> i8:
  -128..127   (256 distinct values)
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what is the range of x plus 1 for a byte x?
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x + 1
  ucas: range it
range of it -> i8:
  -128..127   (256 distinct values)
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what is the square root of x plus 1 where x is a 4-bit unsigned x?
  note: "99" is not one of the 2 choices for "square root" of an integer: read as the floor square root, isqrt
  note: "square root" of an integer: the floor square root, isqrt (kept for this session)
  ucas: it(x: u4) = isqrt(x) + 1
  ucas: show it
it(x: u4) = isqrt(x) + 1
  -> u4
